title: Checking and fixing them
pid: bfe365c2-5b17-4d1f-bc9f-2c1d7ff7ddb8
body: |2-
  At startup the server warns of doubtful attributions among the notes
  of your skgrepos, counted by kind: a recorded remote no loaded skgrepo
  has (perhaps only not loaded, or its remote changed); a recorded name
  now naming a skgrepo with another remote; with no remote recorded, a
  name the config lacks, or one that has a remote now. Each warning says
  how to fix it, with a command naming the server's binary by its
  absolute path. =skg check-attributions CONFIG= prints the same
  without starting a server. =skg fix-attributions CONFIG OLD SKGREPO=
  rewrites every attribution in your skgrepos whose remote hash or
  recorded name is OLD to name SKGREPO as it is now, its name and its
  remote's hash; the original and the commit stay. ('skg' here is the
  built binary, which need not be on the path. From the top of the
  repository, run them as =bash/skg check-attributions CONFIG=, and so
  on: =bash/skg= runs =target/release/skg=, or else =target/debug/skg=.
  Given =--help=, each subcommand describes itself.)
